  "description": "Bike lanes through the week and backroads on the weekend. Happy on-road and off, the Provincial Road 1 can handle your commute, your next group ride, and that bikepacking trip you’ve been thinking about. Outfitted with Shimano's GRX groupset, you get a drivetrain that is tough enough for the trail and incredibly smooth on the road. With 20 gear options right at your fingertips, you can take the edge off hills and put down power, whenever you like. The standard 10mm quick release axles have been swapped out for 12mm thru-axles, reducing flex under hard braking, cornering, and accelerating, giving the bike reliable handling in all conditions. Built on the foundation of an agile steel frame with a stable upright geometry and grippy high-volume tires, the Provincial Road 1 is a solid weekday commuter and excellent weekend adventure buddy.\n\nDesigned to be as fun to ride on your daily commute as it is out bikepacking, the versatile Provincial line is great bang for your buck\n\nReynolds 520 chromoly steel frame with lowered bottom bracket for stable handling\n\nChromoly fork is tough and has the right amount of stiffness for precise handling\n\nFrame and fork are equipped with eyelets for fenders, racks, bottle cages and bag mounts\n\nShimano 10-speed GRX 400 drivetrain pairs 46-30T chain rings with an 11-34T cassette, for fast and reliable shifts on smooth roads and rough trails\n\nShimano GRX 400 hydraulic disc brakes provide outstanding stopping power and modulation regardless of weather\n\nVittoria Terreno Dry tires provide great grip on a variety of surfaces and at 40mm wide, they soak up road and trail vibration. The bike can accommodate up to 45mm tires\n\nFizik Terra Alpaca X5 is 145mm wide, comfortably cradling your sit bones on rough terrain and long rides\n\nPart of MEC’s Provincial collection – a versatile series of bags and bikes that are just as useful on your commute, as they are on your gravel grinds and bikepacking adventures\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes were designed in Canada. From frames, to graphics, to componentry builds, every element of the bike is developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC\n\nDue to challenges with supply chain, components may be substituted for comparable parts at any time. The listed build is how MEC intended your bike to arrive, though the manufacturer may need to make a tweak or two to get you riding sooner",
  "first_year": 2024,
